course: dictionary
lesson: 5742
title: Loudness
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Loudness is how loud a sound is, the strength of a sound that our ears hear. A whisper has little loudness, and a shout has a lot.
explain: In science, loudness depends on the size of the vibrations. Bigger vibrations make a louder sound. Think of a drum: hit it harder and it vibrates more, so it sounds louder.
explain: «In many owls the two ears sit at different heights, so a sound reaches each ear at a slightly different time and loudness.» The owl uses these small differences to work out where a sound comes from, both up or down and left or right.
explain: Loudness is not the same as pitch. Pitch is how high or low a sound is. A tiny whistle can be high-pitched but quiet, and a deep drum can be low-pitched but very loud.
fact: Loudness is how strong a sound is when we hear it.
fact: Loudness depends on the size of the vibrations: bigger vibrations make a louder sound.
fact: Loudness is measured in decibels, written dB.
fact: Very loud sounds can damage your hearing, so wear ear defenders near loud machines.
fact: Loudness is an uncountable noun, so we say "the loudness", not "a loudness".
exercise: What is loudness? | How high or low a sound is | *How strong a sound is when we hear it | How long a sound lasts
exercise: In science, what makes a sound louder? | A higher pitch | *Bigger vibrations | Longer words | Smaller vibrations
exercise: What unit is loudness measured in? | Metres | Grams | Litres | *Decibels, written dB
test: «In many owls the two ears sit at different heights, so a sound reaches each ear at a slightly different time and loudness.» What does the owl compare between its two ears? | How fast it flies | The length of its beak | The colour of its feathers | *The loudness and timing of a sound reaching each ear
test: Ali says a whistle is loud because it is high. Why is that not quite right? | *Loudness is about strength, and pitch is how high or low a sound is | High sounds are always the loudest | Loudness and pitch are the same thing | Whistles are always quiet
exam: Which statement is true? | Loudness is measured in kilograms | *Loudness is how strong a sound is, and pitch is how high or low it is | Loudness and pitch are the same thing | Loud sounds never harm your ears
